  "limitations": [
    "Unchanged retail DI and trig initializer code ran in Melee Unlocked’s Gekko interpreter. Its opcode source was compiled unchanged; paired-single load/store services came from an exact private extraction of that same revision’s runtime implementation, with only symbol names changed for dispatch counting. The repository itself was not edited, and this does not repair or claim Linux portability for the shipped port.",
    "The host was x86-64 Linux with FMA. The project interpreter models the port’s PPC/Jit64 floating-point semantics; this is not a GameCube hardware capture or proof of every hardware rounding detail.",
    "Each case supplies synthetic velocity X/Z and stick X/Z fields in a minimal fighter-state block. This does not execute grounded DI eligibility, controller polling, hitlag timing, collision, or a complete match.",
    "No original DOL or PlCo.dat bytes are included in this JSON."
  ]
